            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 18-year-old female patient, admitted on 23/09/2018 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever. Clinical examination revealed marked tenderness at McBurney's point with rebound tenderness. Blood tests confirmed leukocytosis, and abdominal ultrasound supported the diagnosis of acute appendicitis. The patient was promptly prepared for surgery. A laparoscopic appendectomy was performed on 24/09/2018 without intraoperative complications. The postoperative course was uneventful. Wound care was carried out, adequate analgesia administered, and the patient was mobilized early. Vital signs remained stable throughout. She was discharged home on 26/09/2018 in good general condition with outpatient wound follow-up recommended. Please ensure review within one week post-discharge. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>"
            },
